  "description": "Permanent teeth grow inside the bone beneath the baby teeth; as they push up, the body resorbs the baby tooth's root, which loosens and falls out. Kids have 20 baby teeth and adults up to 32. Enamel is the hardest substance in the body, but bacteria turn sugar into acid that causes cavities, and enamel doesn't grow back. Sharks, by contrast, replace thousands of teeth in their lives. Original 3D animation; not medical or dental advice.",
